 {"id":"fabro-96bd","title":"Implementer prompt: document the ml record flag contract per record type","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:13:20.579Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:32:11.677Z","description":"The implementer's lesson-capture call failed with 'pattern records are missing required flag(s): --name' yet exited 0 with is_error: false (events seq 163-165) — only the stdout text revealed the failure. .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 6 teaches the exact failing form (ml record <domain> --type ... --description ... with no --name). Change: document the exact flag set per record type (pattern requires --name) in step 6, and note the mulch-cli exit-0-on-error bug (same class as sd's fabro-d936) for upstream filing. Expected effect: one fewer failed tool call + LLM round per lesson capture and deterministic error detection.\\nBasis: run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 54612515b569d36aa68872cb119b12ae7f9c4eaf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-9a43","title":"Point reviewer phrase checks at read_file offset/limit when diff line numbers are known","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:40:22.698Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:49:26.064Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md (tool-guidance/verification section), instruct the reviewer to verify phrase-presence claims with read_file offset/limit on the exact lines the diff already names — or pass an explicit max_results to grep — instead of multi-pattern grep alternations. Grounded in run 01M1YWHK6F8F2VZ6F6FZV8A7VE: the reviewer's first grep alternation returned only the line-25 match in truncated output (journal event seq 174, observation 2), forcing a second targeted grep for the carve-out clause — an extra model round-trip (~3–4 s of the reviewer's 23.7 s) for a verification the diff had already localized to lines 25 and 78. Expected effect: one fewer verification round-trip per review of text-edit seeds. Related to open fabro-a0fe (blob reads with read_file offset/limit) but targets the phrase-check guidance — different section, different mechanism (grep-truncation avoidance vs improvised blob reads).\nBasis: run 01M1YWHK6F8F2VZ6F6FZV8A7VE, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 50367ecee388a4806948c80162dc93c2f95f7bb2","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-06e0","title":"develop planner: in-flight PR guard is credential-less and must STAY that way — use fabro_runs_list, remove gh from the toolchain image","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:06:56.713Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:33:12.602Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER DECISIONS 2026-09-08: (D1) Weg A ONLY - extend existing surfaces, NO new tools; (D2) gh REMOVED from the toolchain image by direct revert (commit f00fdb102, capability change without user decision gets reverted per ADR-0019) - image rebuilt and verified (gh absent, sd/rg/just/nu + mise trust intact). SECURITY CONTEXT: the engine injects GITHUB_TOKEN + a git credential bridge into agent shell calls - so the brief gh presence was a write-capable forge client in agent shells, NOT a harmless unauthenticated binary as first assumed; the prohibition rationale is documented on fabro-05d0 and ADR-0019.\n\nREMAINING WORK (this seed): (1) check the OpenAPI/runs list projection - if it lacks pull_request {number, state}, extend it (read-only data enrichment of the existing engine-mediated response); (2) planner guard (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 4 IN-FLIGHT PR CHECK): replace the gh command with fabro_runs_list -> filter runs with open/non-terminal linked PR -> extract seed ids from run goals -> skip matching candidates, journal 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>', continue down sd ready --assignee fabro; remove the gh fail-open clause (no gh exists anymore - the guard must not reference it). Acceptance: a develop pass with a seed whose PR sits open in the gate journals 'skipped: in-flight PR <n>' and claims a DIFFERENT seed - verified live; planner prompt no longer mentions gh; no credential added; no new agent tool exists.","labels":["workflows","revision","engine"]}
-{"id":"fabro-16ff","title":"revisor + reviewer must become security-affine (ADR-0019): capability-affecting ideas get shot down at filing and review time","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:23:10.858Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T15:02:06.311Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER DIRECTIVE 2026-09-08: 'der revisor und der reviewer muessen unbedingt sicherheits-affiner werden, sodass solche ideen von vornherein abgeschmettert werden' - the gh incident (PR #53 baked a forge client into the toolchain image; a follow-up seed proposed GH_TOKEN provisioning) only stayed harmless because credentials happen to be absent from sandboxes - luck, not design. The two autonomous gates must enforce ADR-0019 themselves.\n\nFIX (1) REVISOR file stage (.fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md): add to the seed-intake rules - when a finding or proposed fix direction would ADD/CHANGE/REMOVE a tool, credential, or permission in an agent-reachable surface (Dockerfiles, environment env, tool allowlists, hook configs, new binaries): (a) the seed MUST carry labels needs-user (in addition to revision) and stay for user assignment per ADR-0018 D3; (b) the seed body must cite ADR-0019 and state 'implementation awaits explicit user approval'; (c) the revisor NEVER proposes raw authenticated clients or token provisioning as fix directions - engine-mediated, read-only, extend-existing-tools is the only vocabulary (ADR-0019.2/.3).\nFIX (2) DEVELOP reviewer (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md): add a review axis to the checklist - CAPABILITY DELTA: if the diff touches .fabro/Dockerfile*, env/credential provisioning, tool allowlists, hook configs, or adds binaries/secrets to agent surfaces, verify the seed records an explicit user decision (ADR-0019 citation + approval note); without it, that is a BLOCKING finding -> route Changes requested naming ADR-0019 (a merged capability change without user decision gets reverted). Capability REDUCTIONS (removing tools/credentials, least-privilege narrowing) are fine and welcome - do not block those, just verify they cite their basis.\nAcceptance: revisor files a capability-affecting seed with needs-user + ADR-0019 citation (verifiable on the next such finding); reviewer prompt carries the capability axis; one gate run demonstrates a blocking Changes-requested on a capability delta without recorded approval (test or staged verification).\n\nADDITIONAL EVIDENCE (2026-09-08): the gh incident was WORSE than first diagnosed - the engine injects GITHUB_TOKEN into every agent shell call (resolve_workflow_env) plus a git credential bridge (git_bridge.rs), so the baked gh was fully WRITE-CAPABLE (merge/close/force-push/branch-delete), not a harmless unauthenticated binary. The reviewers approved PR #53 partly because the per-tool-call env injection was invisible from a container-env perspective. The capability axis must teach reviewers to check what the ENGINE hands to agent shells (env injection, credential bridges), not just what the diff itself adds.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
