tools/credentials, least-privilege narrowing) are fine and welcome - do not block those, just verify they cite their basis.\nAcceptance: revisor files a capability-affecting seed with needs-user + ADR-0019 citation (verifiable on the next such finding); reviewer prompt carries the capability axis; one gate run demonstrates a blocking Changes-requested on a capability delta without recorded approval (test or staged verification).\n\nADDITIONAL EVIDENCE (2026-09-08): the gh incident was WORSE than first diagnosed - the engine injects GITHUB_TOKEN into every agent shell call (resolve_workflow_env) plus a git credential bridge (git_bridge.rs), so the baked gh was fully WRITE-CAPABLE (merge/close/force-push/branch-delete), not a harmless unauthenticated binary. The reviewers approved PR #53 partly because the per-tool-call env injection was invisible from a container-env perspective. The capability axis must teach reviewers to check what the ENGINE hands to agent shells (env injection, credential bridges), not just what the diff itself adds.","labels":["workflows","revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-08T15:05:24.310Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-c1bb","title":"Drop current_seed_brief from the develop reviewer node's preamble_allow_keys","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:10:29.339Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:48:00.177Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` (reviewer node), remove `current_seed_brief` from `preamble_allow_keys`. Evidence from run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G: the reviewer preamble carried both the ~2.3 KB `current_seed_brief` and the 8.9 KB evidence capture whose own '== in-progress seed spec ==' section delivered the same spec twice; the duplicated payload blew the 24 KB aggregate inline budget, so the capture rendered as a `blob-ref` and forced a `read_file` detour (reviewer@1). Expected effect: the capture renders inline within the existing budget, one model round-trip removed per review, and the `verification_blocked`-on-blob failure mode disappears. Distinct from open seed fabro-cf3e (raises `preamble_inline_max_kb` 16→32) — this dedupes the spec delivery instead of enlarging the budget; complementary, not superseding. Basis: run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G, workflow version 08846dfb574d2ff5db4e16cc712b4a81c7801307975d397a365a9bc676a3d611, commit e53f85be88b2b379a31ff2822a7eb564e9637fda","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-645d","title":"Implementer prompt: scoped reads via sed -n when the brief pins line anchors","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:10:29.468Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:48:00.284Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` (shell guidance), add: when the brief names line anchors, read with `sed -n '<range>p'` instead of whole-file `cat`. Evidence from run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G: the implementer ran `cat -n` over the entire 111-line `planner.md` (12,096 bytes, event seq 84–85) although the brief pinned the targets ('step 3, line ~35', table ~line 28) and the edit itself used exact-string replace. Expected effect: ~10 KB less context per platform-file edit pass. Reviewer-side analog fabro-9a43 exists; no seed covers the implementer prompt's read discipline — new mechanism on a different node. Basis: run 01M1YY8JJCE31XHSDCZ816634G, workflow version 08846dfb574d2ff5db4e16cc712b4a81c7801307975d397a365a9bc676a3d611, commit e53f85be88b2b379a31ff2822a7eb564e9637fda","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-cf76","title":"Planner: verify spec-named headings/anchors/paths exist in target files before forwarding the brief","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T22:43:30.656Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T23:04:24.572Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 7 (contradiction check), add: when the spec names a heading/anchor/path, confirm it exists in the target file; when it doesn't, annotate the actual location in the brief. Evidence: the run brief forwarded 'checklist gains a CAPABILITY DELTA axis' verbatim, but `reviewer.md` has no heading named 'checklist' (the numbered 'Your job this pass' list is it); the implementer burned a ~14 s / 519-reasoning-token block deciding placement (events seq 95-97). Expected effect: shorter implementer passes and fewer misplacement deviations → fewer Changes-requested cycles (~2.5 min + ~$0.15 each).\nBasis: run 01M1Z017EQK3Q2QCEMTA6XXNSK, workflow version 78ff76ac6dc73632d1cb65e7e2667edcf4d8b52bf90c47667776f8195ee52e5f, commit 91e7b67f7ec6a4f9470dc082882f4cd9fc59b59f","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-07T23:04:24.572Z"}
